# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix, replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader
# refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint, which is what their question (exactness of reuse against a cold twin of the same boot; the platform sequence) does not depend on.
# SR (AFTER THE OWNER APPROVES, on the image B1 builds): the four-card platform replay of the PRODUCTION image: the node agent's serving sequence in a copy of its container
# running the THIN LAYER built on the B1 image (C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer: the step reads the image name from a file the operator writes on the runner; it is never
# committed). The replay sets no profile, so it boots the ship profile BY THE IMAGE DEFAULT, which is why it needs the baked B1 image and so the APPROVED decision (it
# cannot run on the window image, whose default is the approved ship-4 profile). THE RECORDED SOURCE IMAGE: the replay copies the node agent's container from a tracked
# record (scripts/ci/references/c2-serving, the step's --source) and needs that image present on the rig host (c2_platform_replay.source_problem); when the step reports
# 'the source image ... is not on this host', the operator pulls it first - the image name stays out of this file. READ the vLLM subprocess log: '[QWEN-C2] profile
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5: vLLM argv', the OWNER TRAFFIC WAIVER line, the P150x4 mesh, admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED admission
# line and no 262k evidence waiver, prefix installed, the Lever N install and warm lines, the parked build line, every op-fusion lever's engaged line, the :tt alias before
# and after the restart, and no kill-switch line (no levern.off, prefix-reuse.off or parked.off left on the hub). PASS: 'PLATFORM_REPLAY passed=True'. The replay runs the
# base checkpoint (the replay step does not forward the selection); production picks Swift from its node environment, which the replay's copy of the agent's container
# records. The replay turns the session cap off; the cap is read live after the deploy. LEVER READS (the candidate's additions, on top of the ship-4 reads): NP1:
# octo_judge.py --container-log <container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5 clean (the solo rule: at least one "packed padded
# round live=1" line, no "packed padded skipped live=1 eligible=1" line, beside the octo rules) and the NP1 lines in the container log: "[NP1] kv scratch:
# Qwen36ForCausalLM.allocate_kv_cache allocates 1 block(s) beyond the pool vLLM sized (pool 16500 blocks, scratch ids 16500..16500)" once, "[SOLO-PACKED] admitted
# min_users=1 scratch_pages=16500 (owner traffic waiver <id>)" once and, for each of the two M3 blocks, "packed padded block admitted min_users=1 users=4 max_idle=4 ...
# scratch_pages=16500"; the octo block's own admitted line is unchanged (min_users=6, max_idle=2, no scratch pages); EXACT RESUME: "[PINDIAG] prefix: window carry engaged
# undrop=1 carry=1" once (the scheduler graft's install line; a smoke without a salt never reaches it: agent_turns does, and window 2's prefix arm A2 holds the carried hits
# against cold twins); SLICED RESTORE: "host tier restore slice on blocks=512 ms=200" once; GRID13: the "tp4 grid13 engaged" line names all three sub-switches; TIER: the
# "host tier on" line says the 48 GiB budget and the 16 GiB checkpoint store. Measured basis for the estimate: 25 minutes. Duration (estimate): 25 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
